From: CubieBoard4 Build System <build@cubieboard4>
Date: Fri, 7 Mar 2026 07:10:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] mmc: sunxi: skip WAIT_PRE_OVER in clock update when
 mask_data0 is set

When an SD card (mmc0) is inserted at the same time as the BCM4330
WiFi SDIO device (mmc1) is initialising, the WiFi interface fails
to come up on the Allwinner A80 (CubieBoard4).

The symptom is a stream of "fatal err update clk timeout" messages
from mmc1, one every 750 ms, ending in:

  mmc1: Failed to initialize a non-removable card

Root cause
----------
sunxi_mmc_oclk_onoff() issues a clock-update-only command with both
SDXC_UPCLK_ONLY and SDXC_WAIT_PRE_OVER set.  WAIT_PRE_OVER tells
the controller to poll DATA0 until the card signals "not busy"
before completing the command.

The BCM4330 holds DATA0 low while it is held in reset by its
mmc-pwrseq.  Patch 0003 added SDXC_MASK_DATA0 to CLKCR, which is
documented to bypass the DATA0 idle check when writing the clock
configuration register.  However, on the A80 the MASK_DATA0 bit in
CLKCR does not suppress the WAIT_PRE_OVER check in the subsequent
CMDR write: SDXC_START is never cleared, the poll loop always runs
to its 750 ms deadline, and oclk_onoff returns -EIO.

With the SD card absent mmc0 is idle, so there is no electrical load
difference and BCM4330's DATA0 floats high enough for WAIT_PRE_OVER
to clear quickly — WiFi then works.  With the SD card present the
additional bus activity and supply perturbation keeps DATA0 firmly
low, exposing the WAIT_PRE_OVER stall every time.

Fix
---
When mask_data0 is set for a host, the intent is already "do not
wait for DATA0 to be released".  Extending that intent to the CMDR
write — by not including SDXC_WAIT_PRE_OVER — makes the command
complete immediately regardless of the DATA0 state, which is exactly
what mask_data0 was always supposed to achieve.  WAIT_PRE_OVER is
retained for hosts that do not set mask_data0.

Signed-off-by: CubieBoard4 Build System <build@cubieboard4>
---
 drivers/mmc/host/sunxi-mmc.c | 12 +++++++++---
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/mmc/host/sunxi-mmc.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/host/sunxi-mmc.c
@@ -676,7 +676,16 @@ static int sunxi_mmc_oclk_onoff(struct sunxi_mmc_host *host, u32 oclk_en)
 
 	mmc_writel(host, REG_CLKCR, rval);
 
-	rval = SDXC_START | SDXC_UPCLK_ONLY | SDXC_WAIT_PRE_OVER;
+	/*
+	 * When mask_data0 is set, SDXC_MASK_DATA0 in CLKCR tells the
+	 * hardware to bypass the DATA0 idle check in the CLKCR write path,
+	 * but the WAIT_PRE_OVER flag in CMDR re-introduces that same check
+	 * independently.  Skip WAIT_PRE_OVER so that clock-update commands
+	 * complete even when DATA0 is held low (e.g. a WiFi SDIO device in
+	 * reset that cannot release DATA0 before it is powered on).
+	 */
+	rval = SDXC_START | SDXC_UPCLK_ONLY;
+	if (!host->cfg->mask_data0)
+		rval |= SDXC_WAIT_PRE_OVER;
 	mmc_writel(host, REG_CMDR, rval);
 
 	do {
